{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MRK",
  "chapter": 15,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And forthwith in the morning the chief priests held a consultation with the elders and scribes, and the whole council, and bound Jesus, and carried ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " away, and delivered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Pilate.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pilate asked him, Art thou the King of the Jews? And he answering, said to him, Thou sayest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the chief priests accused him of many things: but he answered nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pilate asked him again, saying, Answerest thou nothing? behold how many things they testify against thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Jesus yet answered nothing: so that Pilate marveled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now at ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " feast he released to them one prisoner, whom they desired.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And there was ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " named Barabbas, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who lay",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bound with them that had made insurrection with him, who had committed murder in the insurrection.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the multitude crying aloud, began to desire ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him to do",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as he had ever done to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Pilate answered them, saying, Will ye that I release to you the King of the Jews?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For he knew that the chief priests had delivered him for envy.)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the chief priests moved the people that he should rather release Barabbas to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pilate answered, and said again to them, What will ye then that I shall do ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " whom ye call the King of the Jews?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they cried out again, Crucify him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Pilate said to them, Why, what evil hath he done? And they cried out the more exceedingly, Crucify him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Pilate, willing to content the people, released Barabbas to them, and having scourged Jesus, delivered him to be crucified.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the soldiers led him away into the hall, called Pretorium; and they call together the whole band;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they clothed him with purple, and platted a crown of thorns, and put it about his ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "head",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ",",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And began to salute him, Hail, King of the Jews!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they struck him on the head with a reed, and spit upon him, and bowing ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " knees, worshiped him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they had mocked him, they took off the purple from him, and put his own clothes on him, and led him out to crucify him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they constrain one Simon, a Cyrenian, who was passing by, coming from the country, the father of Alexander and Rufus, to bear his cross.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they bring him to the place Golgotha, which is, being interpreted, The place of a skull.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they gave him to drink, wine mingled with myrrh: but he received ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they had crucified him, they parted his garments, casting lots upon them, what every man should take.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it was the third hour, and they crucified him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the superscription of his accusation was written over, THE KING OF THE JEWS.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And with him they crucify two thieves, the one on his right hand, and the other on his left.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the scripture was fulfilled, which saith, And he was numbered with the transgressors.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they that passed by, railed on him, wagging their heads, and saying, Ah, thou that destroyest the temple, and buildest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in three days,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Save thyself, and come down from the cross.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Likewise also the chief priests mocking, said among themselves with the scribes, He saved others, himself he cannot save.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let Christ the king of Israel descend now from the cross, that we may see and believe. And they that were crucified with him, reviled him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when the sixth hour was come, there was darkness over the whole land, until the ninth hour.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And at the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying, Eloi, Eloi, lama, sabacthani? which is, being interpreted, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And some of them that stood by, when they heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", said, Behold, he calleth Elijah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And one ran and filled a sponge full of vinegar, and put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on a reed, and gave him to drink, saying, Let alone; let us see whether Elijah will come to take him down.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus cried with a loud voice, and expired.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the vail of the temple was rent in two, from the top to the bottom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when the centurion who stood over against him, saw that he so cried out, and expired, he said, Truly this man was the Son of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There were also women looking on at a distance, among whom was Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James the younger, and of Joses, and Salome;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who also, when he was in Galilee, followed him, and ministered to him; and many other women who came with him to Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now, when the evening was come, (because it was the preparation, that is, the day before the sabbath)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Joseph of Arimathea, an honorable counselor, who also waited for the kingdom of God, came, and went in boldly to Pilate, and craved the body of Jesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pilate wondered if he was already dead: and calling the centurion, he asked him whether he had been any while dead.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he knew ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the centurion, he gave the body to Joseph.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he bought fine linen, and took him down, and wrapped ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the linen, and laid him in a sepulcher which was hewn out of a rock, and rolled a stone to the door of the sepulcher.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.15.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.15.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Mary Magdalene and Mary ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the mother",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of Joses, beheld where he was laid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
